+    <h2>Location Usage</h2>
+    <p>Vox.md has two explicit location features. The independent Current Location Capture Bar action requests one location and inserts a Google Maps link in your local draft. Separately, Current Location is off by default and can be enabled per Capture Preset across iOS/iPadOS, Share Sheet, Shortcuts and intents, voice and keyboard-driven preset recording, widgets and controls, Apple Watch captures routed to Markdown, and Mac. A preset can use that one snapshot for a <code>{location}</code> entry-template link without writing additional metadata; Write Location Metadata is a separate opt-in. Watch Recording Only remains a raw audio Files export with no Markdown location surface and does not request location.</p>
+    <p>An enabled preset requests one origin-time location at Send, invocation, or recording stop, depending on the capture source. Exact is the default. City precision rounds latitude and longitude to two decimal places and removes point-of-interest labels before the result is retained; every derived field, template link, and provider link uses the same privacy-adjusted coordinates. Vox.md does not monitor location continuously, run background location tracking, include location in analytics or logs, or send it to a Vox.md server.</p>
     <p>If enabled metadata needs place, city, region, or country, Vox.md uses Apple’s system reverse geocoder. Token-only Current Location skips this lookup. This service is free and requires no API key, but may make a network request to Apple under Apple’s terms. Reverse-geocoding failure does not block Capture; coordinate-only metadata remains available. Vox.md can format links for Apple Maps, Google Maps, and OpenStreetMap without contacting those providers. Only opening a link discloses its exact or rounded coordinates to that provider.</p>
